A command with an unreferenced function under a line directive naming a file the
tree does not hold. The function is reported where the directive renders it, its
column counted on the line that writes it.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

//line grammar.y:10:1
func unused() {}
